.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# The developer's Go workspace is a file about THIS machine, and it wins over
# the module graph: a go.work in the build directory is what `go build` obeys,
# ahead of every replace in every go.mod. Ours carries
#
#     replace github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG => <某人的绝对路径>
#
# so any developer who has a sibling PiG checkout gets an image build that only
# works on their laptop, and the build dies with
#
#     reading <某人的绝对路径>/go.mod: no such file or directory
#
# The portable replacement chain already lives in the go.mod files, which are
# what an image should be built from. It is gitignored for the same reason it is
# excluded here: it is not part of the source, it is part of one checkout.
go.work
go.work.sum

local/
.cache/
tmp/

bin/
dist/stage/
dist/out/
dist/manual-build/

web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

deploy/certs/
deploy/install/certs/
deliverables/

# Deliverables are evidence/documentation, not runtime code.
# Excluding them keeps the image strictly equal to runtime source,
# which lets the frozen declaration hold even after evidence edits.
